# RTL & logical CSS

The app supports RTL locales (`ar`, `fa`). Layout must flip via `dir` on `<html>` and **logical** properties — never via direction checks or physical `left`/`right`.

## Do not

- Compare direction for styling or layout (`dir === 'rtl'`, `getTextDirection()`, `document.dir`, etc.).
- Use physical **left/right** in CSS, Tailwind, or inline styles.
- Use Tailwind physical utilities: `ml`, `mr`, `pl`, `pr`, `left`, `right`, `text-left`, `text-right`, `border-l`, `border-r`, `rounded-l`, `rounded-r`, etc.

## Do

Use **inline / logical** equivalents so LTR and RTL both work:

| Avoid | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `ml-*` | `ms-*` |
| `mr-*` | `me-*` |
| `pl-*` | `ps-*` |
| `pr-*` | `pe-*` |
| `left-*` / `right-*` | `start-*` / `end-*` |
| `text-left` / `text-right` | `text-start` / `text-end` |
| `border-l` / `border-r` | `border-s` / `border-e` |
| `margin-left` / `padding-right` (CSS) | `margin-inline-start` / `padding-inline-end` |
| `left` / `right` (CSS) | `inset-inline-start` / `inset-inline-end` |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div className="ml-4 text-left" />
<div style={{ marginLeft: 8 }} />
{dir === 'rtl' ? 'mr-4' : 'ml-4'}

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="ms-4 text-start" />
<div style={{ marginInlineStart: 8 }} />
<div className="ms-4" />
```

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
.nav-link::after { left: 0; }
[dir='rtl'] .item { margin-right: 1rem; }

/* ✅ GOOD */
.nav-link::after { inset-inline-start: 0; }
.item { margin-inline-end: 1rem; }
```

## Notes

- `mx-*`, `px-*`, `inset-x-*`, `text-center`, and symmetric spacing are fine.
- Ant Design `direction` comes from `CtAntdProvider`; do not mirror RTL in custom CSS with direction branches.
- Prefer `localizeHref()` for links; path locale is separate from layout properties.
- **CtTable** (`ct-table.mdc`): toolbar, row actions, and `ct-table.css` must use start/end — see that rule for widget-specific patterns and Ant Design API exceptions.
